From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: macbox <macbox@localhost>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 16:50:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 06/34] diagnostic:pass timer (M2V_PASS_TIMES)
 and image census (M2V_IMAGE_LOG)

Two default-off diagnostics in metal2vulkan-runtime, to find where a macOS
guest's GPU time goes on the Arrow Lake iGPU (Mesa's INTEL_MEASURE crashes
with this runtime). Each switch is read once; unset, nothing changes: no
query pool, no command, no line. Self-contained: two new modules
(pass_times.rs, image_log.rs) and small hooks, each marked
"LOCAL (Atlas) diagnostic", so the commit can be dropped.

M2V_PASS_TIMES=<dir>: a command buffer begun while <dir>/on exists (checked
once, as it begins recording) gets vkCmdWriteTimestamp(ALL_COMMANDS) pairs
around each unit of GPU work, cut at the recorder's routed entry points so
every recording site is covered: each render pass instance (each instance
of a split pass), each run of dispatches, each run of transfers. Queries
come from the diagnostic's own pools, reset on the host. As the command
buffer completes (completion turn, after its GPU times) one CSV line per
unit goes to <dir>/passes-<pid>.csv:
host_ns,cb_seq,unit_seq,kind,cb_label,encoder_label,attachments,split,draws,gpu_ns
with the kind (render-pass, guest-<encoder>, pass:/internal:<site>), the
queue's label, the encoder's kind and place, each attachment (role, format,
extent, samples, load/store, memoryless, image purpose), the split (i/n,
cause, inline or secondary, why not inline) and the draws/dispatches.

M2V_IMAGE_LOG=<file>: one CSV line per vkCreateImage (purpose, format,
extent, mips, layers, samples, tiling, DRM modifier, usage, create flags,
format list, external handle types, chained structures, memory
requirements), per vkBindImageMemory (the memory's kind: own, host-pages,
dma-buf, dedicated) and per vkDestroyImage: the fields Mesa ANV's CCS
rules read.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
